SUMMARY:Biltmore Estate: Walk the Westover Black Trails
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nLocated at The Inn on Bil
 tmore Estate\, the Westover Black Trails provide access to some of Biltmor
 e's beautiful woodlands. We will loop the Black Trail in a counterclockwis
 e direction.\n\nBiltmore says it is 3.5 miles. The Black Trail is narrow. 
 It is a moderately difficult trail. There is elevation change\, but just a
  bit strenuous. (For those who have walked the Green and Blue Trails\, the
 re is less chance for confusion.)\n\nWhen you drive to the Inn\, you will 
 turn onto its access road. Near the entrance to the Inn is the entrance to
  the parking area. There are two rows of parking\, an upper row closer to 
 the Inn\, and a lower row a little further from the Inn. We will gather on
  the lower row at the far end (away from the Inn).\n\nIf you need a restro
 om prior to the walk\, Antler Hill is very close and there are public rest
 rooms there. No restroom facilities are available during the walk.\n\nDres
 s appropriately for the weather. Tennis shoes are fine\, unless it has rai
 ned a lot recently\, in which case you will want light hiking boots. Walki
 ng sticks are desirable\; I plan to use two. As always\, bring plenty of w
 ater and a protein snack. Dogs on leash are welcome if they are accustomed
  to trail walking. Trail strollers would find this a bit difficult.\n\nThe
 re is a grounds admission fee. We walk at Biltmore several times each year
 \, so an annual grounds pass is highly recommended.\n\nMany regular Biltmo
 re guests have never walked the Westover Trails. I think you will enjoy th
 ese.
