SUMMARY:Millpond Connector at Haywood Community College on National Taco D
 ay
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nAs we enter Leaf Season\,
  the temperature may indeed be cooler. Let's celebrate by going out for ta
 cos after the walk.\n\nTo get to the Millpond Connector from our start poi
 nt\, we will go clockwise on the Bobcat Trail and then take the Kingfisher
  Trail to the Copperhead Trail. When we intersect with the Millpond Connec
 tor\, we will turn left\, finishing the campus loop on the Bobcat Trail. A
 ltogether\, it isn't over 2 miles. Part of the walk is on pavement\, part 
 on well-groomed trail\, and part on not-as-well groomed trail. There is so
 me small elevation change.\n\nAs you enter the campus from Jones Cove Road
 \, go to the first parking lot on the left. We will gather there and then 
 head out.\n\nBe sure to dress for the weather. I'm going to wear tennis sh
 oes\, unless it has rained a lot recently (in which case\, I will wear lig
 ht hiking boots). I plan to bring one walking stick\, just in case. As alw
 ays\, you are urged to bring **plenty of water** and a protein snack. Dogs
  are welcome. Trail strollers should not have any problem. There are no ba
 throoms available on a Sunday afternoon\, so take care of such needs befor
 e you arrive.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/315761287/
