SUMMARY:Sunday Walk at Little Champion Plant in Waynesville
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nOld Timers call this prop
 erty on Old Howell Mill Road near Old Asheville Highway "Little Champion" 
 because the Canton Champion Paper Mill put in this plant to put wax on pap
 er for making milk cartons. The Mill changed hands several times\, but the
  Old Timers kept calling it Little Champion. (Note that Google Maps calls 
 it Evergreen Packaging\, and the sign on the building now says Suzano.)\n\
 nThe 3/4-mile walking track at Little Champion runs by Richland Creek with
  lots of creekside trees\, by fishing spots\, and by a picnic area. There 
 is a bathroom in the middle of the track. We plan to do 4 clockwise laps. 
 (Yes\, you are free to do fewer or even more!) That will make a total of 5
  KM/3.1 miles.\n\nBe sure you enter the property on the Old Asheville High
 way (east) side of the plant (the side with the Suzano sign) on Ken Thomps
 on Drive\, go to the rear of the building\, and then turning left\, go ***
 all the way to the far end of the back of the parking lot\, down by the si
 gn designating the Drop Lot***. It is in that corner of the parking lot wh
 ere we will assemble. (If you go down the stairs into the middle of the tr
 ack\, you will be in the wrong place and will miss where the group is asse
 mbling.)\n\nDress appropriately for the weather\; consider a hat and sunsc
 reen. There is a little hill on each lap\, so some may want walking sticks
  (I plan to use 1 stick). Bring plenty of water and a protein snack. This 
 is a paved track\, so tennis shoes will be fine. Dogs are welcome. Strolle
 rs will have no problem.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/316230402/
